From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:58:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/59] hjviewer: own version info and About links instead of
 RustDesk's

RustDesk asks forks not to use its name or logo. Builds now carry:
- Windows version info naming HJViewer, keeping Purslane's copyright next
  to the HJViewer modifications and the license; the binary keeps
  upstream's file name, so OriginalFilename does too;
- About pages linking to the HJViewer repository as the website and as
  the AGPL Corresponding Source, and to its privacy statement, with the
  modification notice under upstream's copyright line;
- the adaptive launcher icon background color of the HJ monogram.

The icons themselves (an HJ monogram for Android, iOS, Windows, the in-app
logo and res/) are hjviewer's client/overlay files, which
scripts/fetch-upstream.sh copies over the tree: a binary patch would also
carry the upstream logo it replaces.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
